// {{sourceName}}: a starter Malloy model over {{dataPath}}, served by Publisher.
//
// Unlike a package seeded from a format this tool cannot read, the columns below
// were read from the file itself, so this model starts with your data's own
// names rather than with a row count alone. Everything here is a starting point
// and not an answer: the types come from a sample of the rows, the measures are
// the numeric columns that are not identifiers, and the views break the data
// down by the columns with few enough distinct values to chart.
//
// The views count rows on purpose. Which of your numbers is worth charting is
// the one thing a file cannot say, so this does not guess: swap `record_count`
// in any view below for one of the measures above it and you have the chart you
// came for. Delete whatever you do not want; a measure over a column that is
// really a category is the mistake this is most likely to have made.
//
// The profile that produced all of it is written out below, so a wrong guess is
// visible rather than buried: if a column is typed wrong or summed when it
// should not be, that line says why and the fix is to edit the source under it.
//
// Validate edits with compile_model and run new views by name with
// reload_package. The malloy-modeling skill walks through turning a raw table
// into a semantic model.
//
{{profileComment}}

source: {{sourceName}} is duckdb.table('{{dataPath}}') extend {
{{dimensions}}{{primaryKey}}{{measures}}{{views}}}
